1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,060
I love games. Could I make a living making them?

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:06,080
It is okay if you have not chosen a role yet.

3
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:09,720
But enjoying a game and actually making one are a
little different.

4
00:00:09,920 --> 00:00:14,460
Design, programming, and art. Let's start with the
work behind one treasure chest.

5
00:00:15,617 --> 00:00:19,467
Designers decide when a chest opens and what it gives
the player.

6
00:00:19,517 --> 00:00:23,057
What if there is no key? What if the inventory is
full?

7
00:00:23,257 --> 00:00:27,877
Clear writing and logical thinking turn conditions,
outcomes, and exceptions into a shared design.

8
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:31,873
Programmers make those rules work.

9
00:00:32,013 --> 00:00:35,043
Basic C++ teaches you about data and control flow.

10
00:00:35,093 --> 00:00:38,773
Data structures and algorithms help you store and find
items.

11
00:00:39,113 --> 00:00:43,593
If two clicks give two rewards, debugging helps you
find out why.

12
00:00:44,997 --> 00:00:48,857
2D art starts with observation and drawing
fundamentals.

13
00:00:49,017 --> 00:00:53,457
Break a complex chest into simple forms, then
establish proportion and perspective.

14
00:00:53,597 --> 00:00:58,277
Build up light, shade, and color so it remains
readable even at game size.

15
00:00:59,493 --> 00:01:02,583
3D art also relies on understanding form and space.

16
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:06,693
Check proportions from different angles, then refine
the mesh and surface.

17
00:01:06,793 --> 00:01:11,833
Check where the lid pivots. It should not swing around
the wrong point.

18
00:01:12,883 --> 00:01:18,183
Making a living through game development means going a
step beyond playing the games you love.

19
00:01:18,343 --> 00:01:23,003
On a team or on your own, you need to solve the
problems you take on and finish what you make.

20
00:01:23,403 --> 00:01:28,943
Whether you want a studio job or independent
development, start by making and improving something
small.
